111 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 76 0 R
/T (There were no duplicate rows. For missing values, we noticed that the same 59 rows \(about 0.7% of the data\) were missing six of our features at once: depth, SNR, impact, planet radius, star temperature and star radius. Period and duration had no missing values. Since it was only a small group of rows, we filled the gaps with the median. We made sure the median was calculated only from the training data, by doing the filling inside a scikit- learn Pipeline. XGBoost can deal with missing values on its own, so we left them as they were for that model. All our features were already numeric, and we converted the target to 1 for CANDIDATE and 0 for FALSE POSITIVE.)
/E (There were no duplicate rows. For missing values, we noticed that the same 59 rows \(about 0.7% of the data\) were missing six of our features at once: depth, SNR, impact, planet radius, star temperature and star radius. Period and duration had no missing values. Since it was only a small group of rows, we filled the gaps with the median. We made sure the median was calculated only from the training data, by doing the filling inside a scikit- learn Pipeline. XGBoost can deal with missing values on its own, so we left them as they were for that model. All our features were already numeric, and we converted the target to 1 for CANDIDATE and 0 for FALSE POSITIVE.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
