/T (Since the two classes are balanced, we report accuracy. We also report the F1 score for the CANDIDATE class and ROC-AUC. We think ROC-AUC is the most useful one for this problem, because in practice astronomers would use the model to rank signals by how likely they are to be real, and ROC-AUC measures how good that ranking is.)
/E (Since the two classes are balanced, we report accuracy. We also report the F1 score for the CANDIDATE class and ROC-AUC. We think ROC-AUC is the most useful one for this problem, because in practice astronomers would use the model to rank signals by how likely they are to be real, and ROC-AUC measures how good that ranking is.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
