345 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 87 0 R
/T (We met all three of our goals. Using only physical measurements of the transit and the star, our XGBoost model identified false positives with 87% accuracy and a ROC-AUC of 0.93 on stars it had not seen before. This is about 6 percentage points better than the logistic regression baseline, and we did not use any columns from the vetting process. Planet size was the most important feature by far, followed by the number of signals on the same star. Keeping the outliers also turned out to be the right decision, since they were some of the clearest examples of false positives.)
/E (We met all three of our goals. Using only physical measurements of the transit and the star, our XGBoost model identified false positives with 87% accuracy and a ROC-AUC of 0.93 on stars it had not seen before. This is about 6 percentage points better than the logistic regression baseline, and we did not use any columns from the vetting process. Planet size was the most important feature by far, followed by the number of signals on the same star. Keeping the outliers also turned out to be the right decision, since they were some of the clearest examples of false positives.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
