>>
endobj
957 0 obj
<<
/Title (The model made 211 mistakes on the test set. To understand them, we compared the median feature values for the correct and incorrect predictions:)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 837 0 R
/First 1069 0 R
/Last 1070 0 R
/Count -3
/Next 1071 0 R
>>
endobj
958 0 obj
<<
/Title (We also found that some of these "mistakes" might not really be mistakes. Out of the 91 rejected candidates, 77 are still unconfirmed in the final archive. And out of the 120 false positives that the model called candidates, 7 were later confirmed as real planets, so in those cases the model was right and the original label was wrong.)
/Dest [21 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 837 0 R
/Prev 1072 0 R
>>
endobj
959 0 obj
<<
/Title (Bias)
/Dest [21 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 570 0 R
/Prev 838 0 R
/Next 839 0 R
>>
endobj
960 0 obj
<<
/Title (If we had more time, we would try the following:)
/Dest [21 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 839 0 R
/Next 1073 0 R
>>
endobj
961 0 obj
<<
/Title (The model is also specific to Kepler. Another telescope like TESS has different noise and resolution, so the model would need to be retrained to work there.)
/Dest [21 0 R /Fit]
